# The published record is verified BYTE FOR BYTE: CHAIN.jsonl carries the
# sha256 of each snapshot as it sits on disk. Git on Windows rewrites LF to
# CRLF on checkout, which changes those bytes and makes verification fail on a
# record that is perfectly intact -- the worst possible false alarm for a
# document whose entire purpose is being checkable.
#
# So: normalise everything to LF, and mark the record files -text so git never
# touches them at all. A clone must be byte-identical on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.json   -text
*.jsonl  -text
*.csv    -text
*.ots    -text
